From d2cf41cb03376e054404756c4d5f4c452249bc1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 23:03:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] res: bound allocations driven by untrusted asset headers

Every parser here reads data an operator ships, and each of these counts and
sizes was trusted before the first element was read, so tiny files caused fatal
out of memory aborts a recover cannot catch. GRF entries are validated against
the real archive size, PackedSize can no longer exceed AlignedSize, and
decompression is bounded rather than trusting the declared size. ACT, GND, IMF,
RSM, SPR, TGA and GR2 counts are checked against the bytes that remain, GAT
dimensions no longer overflow past their truncation check, and the resource
manager confirms a resolved path stays inside the data directory.
